    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="45">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 45</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="45" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="342" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.7-2"/> man wealdan mæge, ne dýde man æfre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.18"/> on Sunnandæges freolse ænigne forwyrhtne man, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.19"/> he fleo oððe feohte; ac wylde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.20"/> ⁊ healde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> se freolsdæg agan sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="45" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="342" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf man wealdan mæge, ne [dyde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.4-2"/>] man næfre on Sunnandæges freolse ǽnigne forworhtne man, buton he fleo oððe feohte; ac wylde man hine ⁊ healde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> se freol[s]dæg<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.5-2"/> agan sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="45" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="342" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif man wealdan mage, ne dyde man æfre on Sunnandages freolse ænigne forwyrhtne man, buton he fleo oððe feohte; ac wylde ⁊ healde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> se freolsdæg agan sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="45" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="343" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si uitari possit, numquam occidatur aliquis die Dominica morti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.7"/> deputatus (morte forisfactus), nisi fugiat uel repugnet; sed capiatur et seruetur, donec festum transierit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="45" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="343" ed="#liebermann"/>Nullus latro aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.7-3"/> morte condemnatus die Dominico aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.8"/> alio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.9"/> aliquo die<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.10"/> festiuo occidatur, nisi fugere aut pugnare uoluerit; sed custodiatur, quoad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.11"/> usque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_45.lnote.oe.12"/> festiuitas transeat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="45" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="343" ed="#liebermann"/>[45] Si autem fieri potest, nunquam die Dominica quisquam morte dampnatus morti detur (decrete), nisi fugiens aut repugnans sit; sed pocius superetur et seruetur, donec dies festi preterita sit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="45" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="198" ed="#robertson"/>Gyf man wealdan mæge, ne dyde man næfre<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_45.robnote.fn.7"/> on Sunnandæges freolse ǽnigne forworhtne man, buton he fleo oððe feohte, ac wylde man hin<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IICn_45.robnote.fn.8"/>e ⁊ healde þæt se freolsdæg agan sy.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="278" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gyf man wealdan mæge, ne dyde man æfre on Sunnandæges freolse ænigne forwyrhtne man, butan he fleo oððe feohte; ac wylde and healde, þæt se freolsdæg agan sy.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="343" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn es einzurichten möglich ist, richte man niemals in der Sonntagsfeier einen verurtheilten Menschen hin — ausser wenn er flieht oder ankämpft [gegen die Haft] —, sondern bewältige und halte [ihn fest, bis] dass der Feiertag vergangen ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If it can be managed, let no condemned man ever be put to death during the Sunday festival — unless he flees or fights [against arrest] —, but let him be overpowered and held [until] the feast-day has passed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_45.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="199" ed="#robertson"/>If it can be so contrived, no condemned man shall ever be put to death during the Sunday festival, unless he flees or fights, but he shall be arrested and kept in custody until the festival is over.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IICn_45.whinote.n.8"/><pb n="468" ed="#whitelock"/>If it can be arranged, no condemned man should ever be put to death during the Sunday festival, unless he flees or resists; but he is to be seized and kept until the feast-day is over.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="279" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If it can be managed, no one sentenced to death should ever be executed on a Sunday holy day, unless he flees or fights; but he is to be arrested and held until the holy day has ended.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="343"><ref target="clause:EGu_9-1">EGu 9.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. E Gu. 9, 1</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:EGu_9-1">EGu 9.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 45: EGu 9:1</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares EGu 9.1.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 343, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">æfre: næfre B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">wylde: B adds man hine</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">343</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk; lies</hi> de cetero<hi rend="italic">? oder übersetze ‘absichtlich’?</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hk; read de cetero? or translate ‘intentionally’?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">343</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uersetur <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uersetur Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">343</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">festa perterrita <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">festa perterrita Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">342</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später; folgt auf Rasur</hi> me, <hi rend="italic">aber unterstrichen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">later; me follows on an erasure, but is underlined</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">342</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s <hi rend="italic">später</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s later</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">343</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer K; eingeklammertes übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the words before the bracket K; the bracketed words the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">342</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">342</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">næfre <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">næfre Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">342</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">342</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man hine <hi rend="italic">fügt Ld zu</hi> [<hi rend="italic">aus B</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man hine added by Ld [from B]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.7-3" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">343</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">343</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nec <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nec S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">343</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">343</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">f. di. <hi rend="italic">Lb S;</hi> festo <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> die <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">f. di. Lb S; festo without die Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">343</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_45.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">343</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quo <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quo added by Cb</seg></note>
